WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:07.120
Remember the 2005 coming of age superhero movie&nbsp;
“Sky High?” You won’t believe which actor went&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:12.240
on to become an Academy Award winner. Keep&nbsp;
watching to get the dirt on the entire cast.

00:00:14.280 --> 00:00:17.920
Michael Angarano starred in "Sky High" as&nbsp;
Will Stronghold, the son of legendary heroes&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:23.120
The Commander and Jetstream, whose late-blooming&nbsp;
powers land him on the sidekick track at his new&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:23.120 --> 00:00:28.240
super-school. Angarano was only 18 when&nbsp;
"Sky High" first debuted, but by that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.240 --> 00:00:33.920
point he'd already made over half a dozen TV&nbsp;
appearances and landed several film roles,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:33.920 --> 00:00:38.320
including a spot in Cameron Crowe's&nbsp;
music-themed classic "Almost Famous."

00:00:38.320 --> 00:00:43.520
"Sky High" was just the beginning of Angarano's&nbsp;
film career. Over the next decade, he appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:43.520 --> 00:00:48.720
in more than a dozen films, from "The Forbidden&nbsp;
Kingdom" to "The Stanford Prison Experiment."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:48.720 --> 00:00:52.960
He also kept up an impressive television&nbsp;
career with recurring roles in "The Knick,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.960 --> 00:00:58.080
"24," "Will &amp; Grace," and "I'm Dying&nbsp;
Up Here." These days, the 33 year old&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:02.800
can currently be seen as a recurring cast&nbsp;
member in the hit NBC drama "This Is Us."

00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.800
Danielle Panabaker landed the part of plant-loving&nbsp;
Layla in "Sky High," her feature film debut,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:13.440
just a few years into her acting career. After&nbsp;
the film's release, she spent the rest of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:19.040
2000s appearing in films like "Yours, Mine, and&nbsp;
Ours" and the 2009 reboot of "Friday the 13th."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:19.600 --> 00:01:23.680
The early 2010s saw Panabaker&nbsp;
in a number of TV series,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.680 --> 00:01:28.400
most notably "Necessary Roughness"&nbsp;
and FX's western-themed "Justified."

00:01:28.400 --> 00:01:32.560
These days, the 34-year-old Panabaker&nbsp;
is best known for her work in the CW's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:32.560 --> 00:01:37.200
Arrowverse shows as Caitlin Snow and&nbsp;
her supervillain alter-ego Killer Frost.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:37.200 --> 00:01:41.920
She first appeared in the role as a guest star in&nbsp;
the second season of "Arrow," but when CW created&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:47.120
the spinoff show "The Flash," Panabaker joined&nbsp;
as a main cast member. Since then, she's appeared&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:47.120 --> 00:01:52.240
in multiple episodes of other Arrowverse shows,&nbsp;
like "Supergirl" and "DC's Legends of Tomorrow."

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:56.400
Panabaker has been vocal about her desire&nbsp;
to return to the world of "Sky High."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:56.400 --> 00:02:00.080
In 2019, she told the International&nbsp;
Business Times that she would be,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:00.080 --> 00:02:05.280
quote, "a thousand percent" interested in&nbsp;
participating in a sequel. She went on to say,

00:02:05.280 --> 00:02:08.000
"I'd like to think that maybe&nbsp;
they're teachers at 'Sky High,'&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:10.480
because it's been long enough that&nbsp;
they could go back and teach."

00:02:11.200 --> 00:02:15.760
There aren't any solid plans for a sequel&nbsp;
so far, but the door certainly remains open.

00:02:17.336 --> 00:02:22.640
Dee Jay Daniels had a prolific career as a&nbsp;
child actor. He got his start on NBC's "In&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:22.640 --> 00:02:27.680
the House" with LL Cool J, and had a starring&nbsp;
role on "The Hughleys" from 1998 to 2002.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:32.640
"Sky High" was Daniels' first and only&nbsp;
film role. His character Ethan was part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.640 --> 00:02:36.080
of the group of sidekicks at the core&nbsp;
of the film, and he finds a way to help&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:36.080 --> 00:02:41.200
save the day despite his seemingly useless&nbsp;
ability to turn himself into a puddle of goo.

00:02:41.200 --> 00:02:45.920
Despite his impressive and hilarious performance,&nbsp;
Daniels struggled to find more work as he got&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:52.240
older. In an extended 2021 interview with Vlad&nbsp;
TV alongside his former co-star D.L. Hughley,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.400
Daniels opened up about his struggles&nbsp;
with acting. Fans were shocked to see&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:59.840
that, over the years, Daniels had&nbsp;
covered his face with several tattoos,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.640
a decision he claimed to have made partially&nbsp;
in response to his lagging acting career.

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:08.720
Daniels also talked about how his career&nbsp;
was further derailed when he was arrested&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:08.720 --> 00:03:13.440
on suspicion of murder in 2012. It didn't&nbsp;
take long for Daniels to be acquitted,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:13.440 --> 00:03:16.400
but the experience left an&nbsp;
impression on him nonetheless.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:21.280
Nowadays, Daniels is pursuing a rap career, but he&nbsp;
says that he's always open to returning to acting.

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:27.120
Few actors from "Sky High" have kept as busy as&nbsp;
Nicholas Braun, who was just 17 when the film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.120 --> 00:03:32.000
was first released. Braun told BuzzFeed that he&nbsp;
was with two of his friends when he got the call&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:32.000 --> 00:03:36.720
that he'd landed the role of Zach in "Sky High,"&nbsp;
and that he couldn't contain his excitement:

00:03:36.720 --> 00:03:40.720
"I screamed and yelled… I still feel&nbsp;
that way, though, when I get a part."

00:03:40.720 --> 00:03:44.400
If that's the case, Braun has spent a&nbsp;
good amount of time yelling and screaming.

00:03:45.200 --> 00:03:49.040
After "Sky High," Braun spent a handful&nbsp;
of years bouncing between television&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:53.040
shows before landing a recurring role on&nbsp;
"10 Things I Hate About You." From there,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:53.040 --> 00:03:57.200
he turned his attention to the big screen for&nbsp;
films like "The Stanford Prison Experiment" with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:57.200 --> 00:04:02.000
fellow "Sky High" alum Michael Angarano, "How to&nbsp;
Be Single," and "The Perks of Being a Wallflower."

00:04:02.880 --> 00:04:07.760
Braun has kept just as busy in recent years,&nbsp;
starring in two major films — "Zola" and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.760 --> 00:04:13.360
"The Big Ugly" — in 2020 alone. However, Braun&nbsp;
truly broke into the mainstream as fan favorite&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:13.360 --> 00:04:19.840
character Cousin Greg in HBO's "Succession." As&nbsp;
for what's to come in Braun's still-young career?

00:04:19.840 --> 00:04:24.960
"You have to wait and see like everybody&nbsp;
else! But it's awesome, man. It's awesome."

00:04:25.920 --> 00:04:30.960
Who could forget Magenta, the shapeshifter&nbsp;
that can only become a guinea pig? Kelly&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:30.960 --> 00:04:35.520
Vitz's character in "Sky High" had one of&nbsp;
the most memorable powers, and definitely the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:35.520 --> 00:04:40.960
most memorable hair style. Magenta was put on the&nbsp;
sidekick track with the film's other protagonists,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.960 --> 00:04:45.600
and she helped to prove that anyone, no matter&nbsp;
their powers, has the ability to be a hero.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:50.720
Vitz had a short-lived acting career that began&nbsp;
in 2002 when she made a one-line appearance on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:56.000
the Disney Channel show "Lizzie McGuire." Her&nbsp;
next role was in "Sky High," and after that&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.000 --> 00:05:01.680
she landed roles in the horror film "Simon Says,"&nbsp;
"Eye of the Dolphin," "Nancy Drew," and "Teenius."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:01.680 --> 00:05:06.080
Her final film role was as Ailes&nbsp;
Gilmour in the 2010 film "Leonie."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.640 --> 00:05:10.080
That same year, Vitz graduated from&nbsp;
the University of -California Berkeley&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:13.920
with a degree in Public Health, leaving the&nbsp;
film industry to pursue other career goals.

00:05:15.586 --> 00:05:19.120
Steven Strait was fresh out of high school and&nbsp;
just 18 years old when he joined the cast of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:19.120 --> 00:05:24.400
"Sky High" as the aptly named Warren Peace.&nbsp;
"Sky High" was Strait's first feature film,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:24.400 --> 00:05:29.680
and only his second professional acting credit&nbsp;
after a guest appearance on "Third Watch" in 2001.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:30.240 --> 00:05:33.600
Strait followed up the role with a run of&nbsp;
feature films over the next five years,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:33.600 --> 00:05:38.960
which included "The Covenant," "Undiscovered,"&nbsp;
"10,000 B.C.," "Stop-Loss," and "City Island."

00:05:38.960 --> 00:05:43.760
Since 2015, Strait has starred in the&nbsp;
SyFy/Amazon Prime series "The Expanse"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:43.760 --> 00:05:49.840
as the brave starship captain Jim Holden. In&nbsp;
a December 2020 interview with Geeks of Color,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:49.840 --> 00:05:54.640
Strait was asked if he'd ever consider reprising&nbsp;
his role as Warren Peace if Disney revived&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:54.640 --> 00:06:00.000
"Sky High" in some way. Strait said that&nbsp;
he's absolutely open to the idea, adding,

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:02.800
"I loved that experience,&nbsp;
and they're awesome people!"

00:06:04.509 --> 00:06:08.960
Malika Haqq started acting in commercials and&nbsp;
TV shows at a young age. By the early 2000s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:08.960 --> 00:06:11.760
she was used to the grind of&nbsp;
auditions and faceless casting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.680
directors — so much so that when she and&nbsp;
her twin sister Khadijah auditioned for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:20.480
"Sky High," they didn't even realize it&nbsp;
was a feature film. She told E! Online,

00:06:20.480 --> 00:06:23.680
"​​We actually thought the movie was going&nbsp;
to go straight to the Disney Channel,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:27.600
and out of all of those options,&nbsp;
we felt so blessed and overwhelmed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:27.600 --> 00:06:30.640
to learn that [...] 'Sky High'&nbsp;
was going to be our first film."

00:06:30.640 --> 00:06:34.720
Haqq has starred in a few more feature films&nbsp;
in the years since "Sky High": most recently,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:34.720 --> 00:06:40.000
she appeared in the 2016 film "Definitely&nbsp;
Divorcing." However, Haqq is best known&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:40.000 --> 00:06:44.800
for her recurring role in the reality TV series&nbsp;
"Keeping Up with the Kardashians." She's been part&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:44.800 --> 00:06:49.600
of the show since Season 2, and she was a main&nbsp;
cast member on the spinoff series "Dash Dolls."

00:06:51.586 --> 00:06:55.680
Khadijah Haqq McCray's big break also came when&nbsp;
she was cast in "Sky High," and her career since&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:55.680 --> 00:07:00.640
has had a similar trajectory to her sister's as&nbsp;
well. Just one year later, the two went on to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:00.640 --> 00:07:06.160
star in the film "ATL." McCray's last scripted&nbsp;
acting role was in an episode of Kevin Hart's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:11.040
"Real Husbands of Hollywood" in 2013, but like&nbsp;
her sister, she was featured on "Keeping with the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:11.040 --> 00:07:17.120
Kardashians" and co-starred on "Dash Dolls." In&nbsp;
2010, she married NFL defensive end Bobby McCray,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:22.080
and in a January 2021 Instagram post, the&nbsp;
pair announced a new addition to their family.

00:07:22.880 --> 00:07:27.680
Jake Sandvig was only 19 when "Sky High"&nbsp;
arrived in theaters, and it marked his second&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:32.160
feature film. His first, "The Story of Us,"&nbsp;
starred Bruce Willis and Michelle Pfeiffer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:32.160 --> 00:07:37.840
and it came out when Sandvig was just 13 years&nbsp;
old. Despite making appearances in a few TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:43.120
episodes in the meantime, it was after "Sky High"&nbsp;
that his acting career really started to heat up.

00:07:43.120 --> 00:07:46.480
Sandvig had recurring roles on&nbsp;
"Twenty Good Years" and "Cracking Up."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:51.840
His next major film role came in 2010's&nbsp;
"Easy A," and a year later he wrote and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:51.840 --> 00:07:56.320
starred in the film "A Bag of Hammers."&nbsp;
After that, Sandvig returned to television,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:56.320 --> 00:08:02.640
moving from "Weeds" to "CSI" to USA's&nbsp;
"Rush." His most recent roles were in 2017,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:06.720
when he appeared in "Bridal Boot Camp" and&nbsp;
"Hometown Hero" on the Hallmark Channel.

00:08:08.148 --> 00:08:13.120
Will Harris followed up his role as Speed in&nbsp;
"Sky High" with two low-budget features in 2007:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.120 --> 00:08:17.760
"On Broadway" and "Awaken the Dead." After&nbsp;
that, he spent much of his time acting in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.760 --> 00:08:23.520
some of the most popular shows of the decade, such&nbsp;
as "CSI," "Friday Night Lights," and "Community."

00:08:23.520 --> 00:08:27.600
Harris' pace has never slowed down. While&nbsp;
continuing to make guest appearances on a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:27.600 --> 00:08:32.480
variety of shows throughout the 2010s, he's&nbsp;
also lent his talents to the films "In Time"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:32.480 --> 00:08:38.000
and "Sharon 1.2.3." He's had a busy 2021: he&nbsp;
made a guest appearance on ABC's "The Rookie,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:43.040
and he took part in the crime drama "No Man of&nbsp;
God" and the horror film "Shot in the Dark."

00:08:43.840 --> 00:08:48.240
Mary Elizabeth Winstead, who played Gwen&nbsp;
in "Sky High," is probably the film's most&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:48.240 --> 00:08:54.080
recognizable cast member that isn't Kurt Russell.&nbsp;
Though she began her acting career in 1997,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:54.080 --> 00:08:58.640
"Sky High" was only Winstead's third feature&nbsp;
film. Her role in the film gave Winstead&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:58.640 --> 00:09:03.360
the opportunity to display her range, from&nbsp;
kind-hearted classmate to diabolical villain.

00:09:03.360 --> 00:09:07.120
Winstead followed up "Sky High" with&nbsp;
"Final Destination 3," and horror&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:07.120 --> 00:09:12.080
has been part of her wheelhouse ever since.&nbsp;
She's made appearances in "Abraham Lincoln:&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:12.080 --> 00:09:16.400
Vampire Hunter" and "10 Cloverfield&nbsp;
Lane," as well as iconic pop culture&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:16.400 --> 00:09:19.840
films like "Scott Pilgrim vs.&nbsp;
the World" and "Birds of Prey."

00:09:19.840 --> 00:09:23.280
Winstead's most recent leading&nbsp;
role was as the titular assassin&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:27.840
in the Netflix action film "Kate." While&nbsp;
speaking with Collider about the movie,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:27.840 --> 00:09:31.760
Winstead took a moment to reflect on&nbsp;
her beloved performance in "Sky High,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:31.760 --> 00:09:35.840
and speculated about what role her character&nbsp;
would take in a sequel film, saying,

00:09:36.480 --> 00:09:39.840
"[Gwen is] still operating&nbsp;
as a supervillain, for sure."

00:09:39.840 --> 00:09:43.040
"I went through puberty twice for this?"

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:48.640
Kevin Heffernan had already starred in "Super&nbsp;
Troopers" by the time he got a part in "Sky&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:48.640 --> 00:09:52.720
High," and he put his comedic experience&nbsp;
to excellent use by bringing school bus&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:52.720 --> 00:09:57.040
driver Ron Wilson's unabashed excitement&nbsp;
to life. Just like the audience watching&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:09:57.040 --> 00:10:02.480
"Sky High," Ron is an enthusiastic fan of&nbsp;
all things superhero. Getting to "drive"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:02.480 --> 00:10:06.560
the next generation of heroes to Sky High&nbsp;
every morning is a dream come true for Ron,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:06.560 --> 00:10:10.160
and by the end of the film, he gets&nbsp;
his own opportunity to be a hero.

00:10:10.160 --> 00:10:15.120
In the years since "Sky High," Kevin Heffernan has&nbsp;
continued putting his talents to work in comedies&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:20.400
of all stripes. He's made guest appearances&nbsp;
in some of the biggest sitcoms of the past two&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:25.280
decades — "Curb Your Enthusiasm," "How I Met Your&nbsp;
Mother," and "Veep," to name a few — and his film&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:30.400
roles, which include "Strange Wilderness" and "The&nbsp;
Babymakers," have had a similarly comedic bend.

00:10:30.400 --> 00:10:34.640
Currently, fans can catch up with&nbsp;
Heffernan on truTV's "Tacoma FD."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:36.960
He created the series with&nbsp;
the help of Steve Lemme,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:36.960 --> 00:10:41.280
and the two of them lead the show as Chief&nbsp;
Terry McConky and Captain Eddie Penisi.

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:46.960
As one of the few adults cast in "Sky High,"&nbsp;
Jim Rash already had over a decade of acting&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:46.960 --> 00:10:51.760
experience under his belt when he signed on to&nbsp;
play Mr. Grayson and his alter ego, Stitches.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:52.480 --> 00:10:57.360
Most notably, from 2002 through 2006,&nbsp;
he had a recurring role as Fenton on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:10:57.360 --> 00:11:01.840
"That '70s Show." Though he'd maintained&nbsp;
a steady stream of roles up to that point,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:01.840 --> 00:11:04.960
Rash's career was in many&nbsp;
ways just getting started.

00:11:04.960 --> 00:11:09.600
Four years after "Sky High," Rash joined the&nbsp;
cast of "Community" as Dean Craig Pelton,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:09.600 --> 00:11:14.480
a role that he would continue playing throughout&nbsp;
the show's entire six-season run. He's also made&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:14.480 --> 00:11:19.120
non-stop appearances in TV shows and movies for&nbsp;
the past decade: most recently, he's been the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:24.400
voice of Flix in "Star Wars Resistance" and the&nbsp;
Riddler in the animated "Harley Quinn" series.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:24.400 --> 00:11:29.280
Rash is also the only member of the "Sky High"&nbsp;
cast to have won an Academy Award so far,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:29.280 --> 00:11:34.160
having received the Best Adapted Screenplay&nbsp;
Oscar for "The Descendants" in 2012.

00:11:34.880 --> 00:11:39.680
Dave Foley is probably best known for the&nbsp;
work he did before "Sky High." Foley and&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:39.680 --> 00:11:44.480
Kevin McDonald formed sketch comedy troupe&nbsp;
"The Kids in the Hall" in 1984, and their TV&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:44.480 --> 00:11:51.200
show of the same name ran from 1988 to 1995. "The&nbsp;
Kids in the Hall" is set for a revival in 2022,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:51.200 --> 00:11:55.440
but Foley has kept himself plenty busy&nbsp;
in the years since it went off the air.

00:11:55.440 --> 00:11:59.280
In addition to starring in the occasional&nbsp;
feature film, Foley has spent a majority of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:11:59.280 --> 00:12:02.800
his time making guest appearances&nbsp;
on everyone's favorite TV shows.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:02.800 --> 00:12:06.960
He's taken on live-action series like "It's&nbsp;
Always Sunny in Philadelphia" and "Veep,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:06.960 --> 00:12:11.840
as well as animated shows like "Robot&nbsp;
Chicken" and "Dan Vs." In 2021 alone,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:15.920
Foley has made guest appearances in "Young&nbsp;
Sheldon," "Call Your Mother," "Superstore,"&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:12:15.920 --> 00:12:21.440
and "The Morning Show." There isn't a style of&nbsp;
comedy that Foley can't seem to handle perfectly.

